{
  "uid": "aiops-workshop",
  "title": "AIOps workshop",
  "tags": ["aiops", "workshop"],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "editable": true,
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "time": { "from": "now-30m", "to": "now" },
  "refresh": "10s",
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "iface",
        "label": "Interface",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
        "query": "label_values(node_network_receive_bytes_total, device)",
        "refresh": 1,
        "includeAll": false,
        "current": { "text": "en0", "value": "en0" }
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Live metrics from node_exporter",
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 0 },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What this row is for",
      "gridPos": { "h": 5, "w": 6, "x": 0, "y": 1 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "These panels query **Prometheus**, which scrapes `node_exporter` on your own machine. Nothing here comes from the course; the exporter is the official binary and the metrics are your real interface counters.\n\nEvery expression uses `rate()` because the underlying series are counters. Removing `rate()` gives a line that only ever climbs, which is the first thing to check when a panel looks wrong.\n\nDownload something large and watch all three panels move together."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Throughput, receive and transmit",
      "description": "rate() over a counter. Compare with traffic_bps in Lab 01, which is the same idea computed as a per-interval delta in pandas.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 5, "w": 9, "x": 6, "y": 1 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": { "unit": "Bps", "custom": { "fillOpacity": 8, "lineWidth": 1 } },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "rate(node_network_receive_bytes_total{device=\"$iface\"}[1m])",
          "legendFormat": "receive",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "rate(node_network_transmit_bytes_total{device=\"$iface\"}[1m])",
          "legendFormat": "transmit",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Mean packet size",
      "description": "Bytes per second divided by packets per second. Lab 01 event B moves this hard while leaving throughput almost flat.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 5, "w": 9, "x": 15, "y": 1 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": { "unit": "bytes", "custom": { "fillOpacity": 0, "lineWidth": 1 } },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "(rate(node_network_receive_bytes_total{device=\"$iface\"}[1m]) + rate(node_network_transmit_bytes_total{device=\"$iface\"}[1m])) / clamp_min(rate(node_network_receive_packets_total{device=\"$iface\"}[1m]) + rate(node_network_transmit_packets_total{device=\"$iface\"}[1m]), 1)",
          "legendFormat": "avg packet bytes",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "single" }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Lab results, read straight from outputs/workshop/*.csv",
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 6 },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Where this data comes from",
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 6, "x": 0, "y": 7 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "These panels query the **Lab outputs** datasource, which is the Infinity plugin reading CSV over HTTP.\n\nStart the file server from the repository root before opening this dashboard:\n\n```bash\npython -m http.server 8080 \\\n  --directory outputs/workshop\n```\n\nRe-run a notebook cell, refresh the panel, and the line changes: the notebook writes a file and Grafana reads it over HTTP.\n\nEmpty panels almost always mean the file server is not running. Open <http://localhost:8080> and check."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Lab 01  traffic against its rolling robust baseline",
      "description": "outputs/workshop/lab01_baselines.csv. The shaded band is the baseline plus and minus three MAD; watch it widen around an event it failed to catch.",
      "datasource": { "type": "yesoreyeram-infinity-datasource", "uid": "lab-outputs" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 9, "x": 6, "y": 7 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": { "unit": "Bps", "custom": { "fillOpacity": 0, "lineWidth": 1 } },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": { "id": "byName", "options": "robust_hi" },
            "properties": [
              { "id": "custom.fillBelowTo", "value": "robust_lo" },
              { "id": "custom.fillOpacity", "value": 16 },
              { "id": "custom.lineWidth", "value": 0 }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": { "id": "byName", "options": "robust_lo" },
            "properties": [{ "id": "custom.lineWidth", "value": 0 }]
          }
        ]
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "type": "csv",
          "source": "url",
          "format": "table",
          "parser": "backend",
          "url": "http://localhost:8080/lab01_baselines.csv",
          "url_options": { "method": "GET" },
          "columns": [
            { "selector": "timestamp", "text": "time", "type": "timestamp" },
            { "selector": "traffic_bps", "text": "traffic_bps", "type": "number" },
            { "selector": "robust_center", "text": "robust_center", "type": "number" },
            { "selector": "robust_lo", "text": "robust_lo", "type": "number" },
            { "selector": "robust_hi", "text": "robust_hi", "type": "number" }
          ],
          "filters": []
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Lab 02  anomaly score, and what survived the policy",
      "description": "outputs/workshop/lab02_detection.csv. score_max is Layer 1; label is Layer 2 after consecutive confirmation; alert is Layer 3 after the full policy.",
      "datasource": { "type": "yesoreyeram-infinity-datasource", "uid": "lab-outputs" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 9, "x": 15, "y": 7 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none",
          "custom": { "fillOpacity": 0, "lineWidth": 1, "thresholdsStyle": { "mode": "line" } },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "transparent", "value": null },
              { "color": "red", "value": 4 }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "type": "csv",
          "source": "url",
          "format": "table",
          "parser": "backend",
          "url": "http://localhost:8080/lab02_detection.csv",
          "url_options": { "method": "GET" },
          "columns": [
            { "selector": "timestamp", "text": "time", "type": "timestamp" },
            { "selector": "score_max", "text": "score_max", "type": "number" },
            { "selector": "label", "text": "label", "type": "number" },
            { "selector": "alert", "text": "alert", "type": "number" }
          ],
          "filters": []
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Notebook charts, served as PNG from the same folder",
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 14 },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Lab 01  four baselines on one traffic series",
      "description": "Written by the notebook with fig.savefig(). A core Text panel in markdown mode will render any image the file server can reach.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 12, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 15 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "![four baselines](http://localhost:8080/lab01_baselines.png)\n\nThe rolling band swallows the event it is supposed to flag. The seasonal band does not."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 22,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Lab 02  score, label, alert",
      "description": "Written by the notebook with fig.savefig().",
      "gridPos": { "h": 12, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 15 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "![three layers](http://localhost:8080/lab02_layers.png)\n\nFind the isolated breach that produced no label and no alert. That gap is the deadband."
      }
    }
  ]
}
